<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- ============================================================
         LAUNCHER ICON PARAMETERS - ROUND 26, v0.9.11.
         Variant "Ollidar llama" (owner-supplied artwork).

         This file is the SINGLE source of truth for the adaptive icon's
         background colour. Nothing else hard-codes it: the adaptive-icon
         definitions in mipmap-anydpi-v26/ reference @color/ic_launcher_background
         directly, so re-tinting the icon is a one-line change here.

         Colours used ONLY by the launcher icon live in this file. App theme
         colours belong in themes.xml - do not cross-reference the two, or a
         theme tweak will silently restyle the launcher icon.
         ============================================================ -->

    <!-- The cream plate the llama is drawn on, sampled from the owner's
         master-flat-square-1024.png (modal interior colour, #F2F1EC).

         It matches the foreground layer's own cream EXACTLY, and that is
         load-bearing rather than tidy: the foreground is a raster tile of the
         artwork that stops well short of the canvas edge, so background and
         foreground meet at a visible seam unless the two creams are the same
         value. Launcher parallax slides the layers against each other, which
         would make any mismatch move. Re-sample this if the artwork is
         re-exported.

         NOT the orange frame colour (#E55B2A). The master's orange frame is a
         FRAME, and the launcher already draws one - its own mask. Painting the
         plate orange and insetting the cream would double-frame the mark and
         put an unpredictable-width ring under every OEM mask shape. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#F2F1EC</color>
</resources>
